            <ArticleTitle>[The incidence and treatment effect on headache in patients with craniomandibular disorders].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>123-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After a short review of the recent literature on headache the close relationship between headache and craniomandibular disorders was studied. In a total of 116 patients with craniomandibular disorders in the Stomatognathic Physiology Clinic of the Dental School of the University of Athens, 73 patients (62.9%) were found suffering from headache. In most of the patients the headache subsided after the treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
